/* Logic:

1. Initialize `j = 0`. It represents the position where the next non-zero element should be placed.
2. Traverse the array using pointer `i` from index `0` to `n-1`.
3. Check whether `nums[i]` is non-zero.
4. If it is non-zero:
   - Swap `nums[i]` with `nums[j]`.
   - Increment `j` to the next available position.
5. If it is zero, skip it and continue.
6. After traversing the complete array, all non-zero elements will be at the beginning, and all zeroes will be at the end.

### Complexity

- Time: $O(n)$
- Space: $O(1)$
- Technique: Two Pointers (Slow & Fast Pointer).

Key idea: `i` searches for non-zero elements, while `j` maintains their correct positions.
*/

class Solution {
public:
    void moveZeroes(vector<int>& nums) {

        int j = 0; // Tracks the position for the next non-zero element

        // Traverse the entire array
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            // Check if the current element is non-zero
            if (nums[i] != 0) {

                // Move the non-zero element to position j
                swap(nums[i], nums[j]);

                // Move j to the next available position
                j++;
            }
        }
    }
};
